WEBVTT

00:01:27.416 --> 00:01:31.170
There’s no point in being the first
if we’re also the last.

00:01:31.879 --> 00:01:34.006
So here are three ways that all of us,

00:01:34.006 --> 00:01:37.260
whether you’re a first in your company
or a part of a deep legacy,

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:38.511
can embrace this spirit.

00:01:38.845 --> 00:01:39.846
One:

00:01:39.846 --> 00:01:41.264
question your surroundings.

00:01:41.722 --> 00:01:42.723
One of the benefits,

00:01:42.723 --> 00:01:44.725
and really the consequences of privilege,

00:01:44.725 --> 00:01:47.478
is being around people
whose experiences mirror your own.

00:01:47.895 --> 00:01:49.397
So when you're at the table,

00:01:49.397 --> 00:01:52.441
I want to ask you to really examine
who’s there with you,

00:01:52.441 --> 00:01:53.985
and even more importantly,

00:01:53.985 --> 00:01:55.027
who isn’t.

00:01:55.903 --> 00:01:57.155
Do you see women,

00:01:57.155 --> 00:01:58.156
people of color,

00:01:58.156 --> 00:01:59.407
people with disabilities,

00:01:59.407 --> 00:02:03.202
people who look like your customers,
clients, patients and community?